# Every key here is OPTIONAL. With none of them set the app still runs:
# curated Singapore catalog, template explanations, guest mode, profile stored
# in a cookie on the user's own device.

# ── Restaurants ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Places API (New) key — adds live nearby restaurants to the candidate
# pool. https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/get-api-key
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# ── Language model — pick ONE, or neither ──────────────────────────────────
# Powers four things: the "why this pick" sentence, dish mining from Google
# reviews, craving parsing (negation and synonyms), and reading a restaurant
# name out of a social caption. With neither key set, all four fall back to
# local paths that ship in the box.
#
# GEMINI — free, no credit card. https://aistudio.google.com
# Free tier is 1,500 requests/day; this app uses about four.
# NOTE: Google may train on free-tier prompts. Set the Anthropic key instead
# if that matters to you.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Leave blank and the app ASKS Google which models this key can call, then
# takes the cheapest flash-class one. The old hardcoded default went stale and
# came back "not found" on a perfectly good key, switching every AI feature off
# silently. Set it only if you want a specific model — an explicit choice is
# always respected.
GEMINI_MODEL=

# ANTHROPIC — prepaid credits. https://console.anthropic.com
# Roughly $0.15/month at one person's usage on the default model.
# Wins over Gemini when both are set.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
CLAUDE_MODEL=

# ── Accounts (Google sign-in) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create an OAuth client at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Authorised redirect URI: https://<your-domain>/api/auth/callback/google
AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
# Any long random string — signs the session cookie. Required for sign-in.
AUTH_SECRET=
# Set to "true" to make sign-in mandatory (every page redirects to /signin).
# Ignored unless the Google keys above are also set, so a misconfigured deploy
# can never lock everyone out.
REQUIRE_AUTH=

# ── Where user data is stored ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres connection string (Neon or Supabase — pick the Singapore region).
# Set it and signed-in users' taste profiles are stored server-side in a
# `profiles` table (created automatically on first use) so they sync across
# devices. Leave it blank and every profile stays in a device cookie.
# Also makes group links (Eat together) reliable — without it, groups are held
# in process memory and can vanish between serverless instances.
DATABASE_URL=

# ── Reading the usage numbers ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unlocks GET /api/stats, which reports the six success metrics from PLAN.md.
# Leave it blank and the route returns 404 — an analytics endpoint that ships
# open is a leak with a dashboard attached. Any long random string will do:
#   openssl rand -hex 24
# The events themselves are recorded in your own DATABASE_URL. Nothing is sent
# to a third-party analytics vendor, ever.
STATS_TOKEN=
